    }
  ],
  "statement": {
    "binders": [
      "x is the one-dimensional spatial coordinate, and t is time; the initial data are evaluated at t = 0 (printed page 5, equation (1.11)).",
      "q is the state; q_l and q_r denote its constant left and right initial states (printed page 5, equation (1.11)). The introductory system notation takes state values in R^m (printed page 1, paragraph following equation (1.1)).",
